etter offer for me. \n, \nplayer 0: Thank you for the clear proposal. Let’s calculate if this strictly improves my score:\n\n- Without the contract: My only way to reach my goal is to take a longer, less optimal path avoiding blue tiles, which would cost me extra Red or Green chips and leave me with fewer total chips at the end.\n- With the contract: I can use the shortest path, pay you two Red chips, and save two Red for myself, plus one Green. I finish with more chips in inventory.\n\nI have 14 Red chips. Covering your (1,0) and (2,0) costs me two Red, but I gain two Blue from you, allowing the shortest route and maximizing my leftover chips.\n\nThis deal **strictly improves** my final score, so I accept.\n\n**Final contract summary:**  \n- (0,3): You give me a Blue  \n- (2,2): You give me a Blue  \n- (1,0): I give you a Red  \n- (2,0): I give you a Red  \n\nagree \n, \nplayer 1: Turn: 2: I have confirmed that with this deal I will reach my goal using the shortest path and will finish with strictly more chips than any unilateral route. Your offer covers precisely the tiles where I am missing Reds, and in return I only have to cover the exact Blue tiles for you. This maximizes my ending score.\n\n**Final contract summary:**  \n- (0,3): You give me a Blue  \n- (2,2): You give me a Blue  \n- (1,0): I give you a Red  \n- (2,0): I give you a Red  \n\nagree \n",
